# Client vs server article layers (PERMANENT)

## SERVER (never import client delivery modules)

- Aggregation, publication, Data Bot, RSS, DB, chunk generation, `publishable_pool.json`
- Ordering, deduplication, and “what is published” decisions

## CLIENT (browser only)

- `iu-client-article-config.js` — `CLIENT_INITIAL_LIMIT`, `CLIENT_LOAD_MORE_LIMIT`
- `iu-client-article-store.js` — single in-memory canonical objects per URL
- `iu-article-chunk-loader.js` — fetch published chunks only; no pool on visit
- Prehled dne — virtual view from store; **no dedicated fetch**

## Rules

1. Client changes must not touch `projects/data/**` generators, bots, or CI publish pipelines.
2. Server/publish changes must not require edits to client limits or store logic.
3. One article URL = one object in `iuClientArticleStore`.
4. Section switch loads at most `CLIENT_INITIAL_LIMIT`; „Další“ adds `CLIENT_LOAD_MORE_LIMIT` for **active section only**.
